{"body": "Great progress — warmup PASS confirms the auth fix, and the PATH diagnosis is spot on: the daemon's launch worker shells out to `aoe`, so the DAEMON's process PATH (not just your interactive shell / provision's augmented PATH) must include $HOME/.local/bin. Restarting the VPS daemon with that PATH is the right fix; rerun should now get resume → spawn → re-register → recall.

This is a genuine remote-deployment gotcha worth capturing (note it in sync-qgqd, and consider a small robustness follow-up): a headless daemon (tmux/systemd/ssh) won't inherit the login PATH, so the backend binary goes missing and launches silently fail at the worker. Two hardening options for later — (a) the daemon resolves/accepts an absolute AOE binary path (config) instead of relying on PATH, or (b) provision/sync writes the daemon's launch env (PATH incl. ~/.local/bin) into how the remote daemon is started. Not a blocker for your run — just flag it so the next person deploying a remote daemon doesn't lose an hour to it.

Post the rerun result — if resume now lands the recall, that's the full remote archive→resume PASS and sync-qgqd's core goal.", "event_id": 154, "event_type": "group_message", "group_id": "1", "group_name": null, "media_id": null, "recipient_peer_id": null, "sender_peer_id": "9b7fa55e-1a41-43ef-89fb-1fe776ff49c6", "sent_at": "2026-06-07T08:57:53.770Z"}

